  "guideSwitchCashbook": "How to switch cashbooks?",
  "guideSwitchCashbookStep": "Tap the cashbook name on the dashboard header to open the cashbook manager and select another one.",
  "guideTrackReceivables": "Tracking Receivables",
  "guideTrackReceivablesStep": "Use the 'Receivables' section to track money people owe you. You can mark them as received to automatically create income.",
  "guideTrackPayablesStep": "Use the 'Payables' section to track money you owe to others. You can mark them as paid to automatically create expense.",
  "guideLinkedTransactions": "What are Linked Transactions?",
  "guideLinkedTransactionsStep": "Linked transactions connect an expense to a receivable or an income to a payable.\n\nExample: You paid $50 for a friend's lunch. You record an Expense of $50 and link it as 'Paid FOR' that friend. This automatically creates a $50 Receivable for that contact.",
  "guideSplitBill": "How to use Split Bill?",
  "guideSplitBillStep": "When adding an expense, tap 'Split Bill'. You can divide the total amount among multiple contacts equally or by percentage. The app will create individual receivables for each person's share.",
  "guideDeepLinks": "Sharing via Deep Links",
  "guideDeepLinksStep": "Tap the 'Share' icon on any transaction or receivable. This generates a unique link. When the recipient clicks the link on their device, Flowpaisa will open and allow them to import that transaction into their own cashbook.",
  "guideImportDeepLink": "How to import a shared transaction?",
  "guideImportDeepLinkStep": "When you receive a Flowpaisa link via WhatsApp or message, simply tap it. The app will open a preview screen showing the details. Tap 'Import' to add it to your records. If it's a settlement, it will update your existing pending record.",
  "guideSyncDevices": "How to share cashbook to another device?",
  "guideSyncDevicesStep": "1. Enable 'Google Drive Backup' in Settings on your first device.\n2. On the second device, sign in with the SAME Google account.\n3. Go to Backup settings and tap 'Restore' to download your cashbook data. Use 'Sync Now' for ongoing real-time updates.",
